# Claude Code workflow reference

Env-specific facts and decisions only, each at its current state with a dated
annotation. Generic harness behavior is injected into every session or
answerable live via the claude-code-guide agent; measurements, research and
audit baselines live in the chezmoi repo's `docs/agents-audit-log.md`. If
behavior seems changed, verify with that agent and update this file.

## Models (last verified 2026-09-25)

- Settings pin the driver (`model` key) to `{{ index .subagent_tiers.claude .agents.claude.defaults.tier }}`;
  effort `{{ .agents.claude.defaults.reasoning_effort }}` is pinned per model under `modelSettings` for both
  `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.top }}` and `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`, so a `/model` escalation keeps
  it. The 1M window is the default on Opus 4.7+ and Fable, no
  `[1m]` suffix. Opus 5.5 needs CLI ≥ 2.1.280; changing channel
  does not move the pin.
- Escalate effort first: `/effort xhigh` keeps the prompt cache. `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`
  is escalation-only (since 2026-09-25): for an ambiguous root-cause or
  architecture problem where the driver at higher effort fell short, start a
  fresh session with `claude --model {{ .subagent_tiers.claude.frontier }}`. Do not `/model` a grown
  session: each model has its own cache, so the next request re-reads the
  whole history uncached at the frontier rate; `/model <name>` also saves it
  as the default in `~/.claude/settings.json` until the next apply (decision
  2026-09-26; evidence and reversal triggers in the audit log).
- Managed roles below render from `subagents` in agents.yaml, which records
  each choice's why; reversal gates are in the audit log. Pins do not follow
  `/model`; a child without explicit effort inherits session effort.

| role | model | effort |
|---|---|---|
{{ range $name, $role := includeTemplate "claude-roles" (dict "root" .) | fromJson -}}
| {{ $name }} | `{{ $role.model }}` | {{ $role.effort | default "—" }} |
{{ end }}
- `general-purpose` and `Plan` are managed overrides of the built-ins
  (2026-09-25). `CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL` (`{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.top }}`)
  remains only the fallback for the built-in `claude` type, plugin agents,
  workflow agents and teammates;
  leave its `_FORCE` variant unset, it would erase specialist pins. Forks
  continue the parent model; the guide uses Haiku, the statusline helper Sonnet.
- Resolution order (since 2.1.251): per-call `model`, frontmatter (`inherit` =
  main conversation), the env fallback, main conversation; no role uses `inherit`.
{{- $bare := list }}{{ $scoped := list }}{{ $frontierDeny := "" }}
{{- range .agents.claude.denied_tools }}{{ if hasPrefix "Agent(model:" . }}{{ $frontierDeny = . }}{{ end }}{{ if contains "(" . }}{{ $scoped = append $scoped . }}{{ else }}{{ $bare = append $bare . }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
- The `{{ $frontierDeny }}` deny rule is the per-call frontier guard;
  `~/.claude/hooks/deny-frontier-child.mjs` is the legacy second guard until
  the owner's trial of that rule deletes it. Neither sees a third-party
  definition declaring `model: inherit`, and neither proves actual routing.
- After each CLI update, dispatch one unpinned child and one with an explicit
  `{{ .subagent_tiers.claude.top }}` override and verify `message.model`, not
  self-report; routing issue history and the latest sample are in the audit log.
- Every custom subagent loads `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (driver-only rules sit under
  "session driver") and draws the same Max pools (5-hour window, shared weekly
  pool; Fable's 50% weekly cap is shared, not reserved); check `/usage`.
- `cross-model-review` / `cross-model-advice` are read-only GPT consultations;
  decisions stay in Claude, triggered by risk or breadth (decision 2026-09-03).

## Local-only surface (decision 2026-09-21)

- The CLI carries no claude.ai-product surface: account skill and plugin sync,
  claude.ai connectors and Remote Control are off in settings; the cron
  scheduler is disabled by env;
  `{{ $bare | join "`, `" }}` are bare-denied, which removes them from the tool
  list; `{{ $scoped | join "`, `" }}` are scoped denies that block only the
  matching call. Bundled skills hidden via `skillOverrides` and the
  deny list live in agents.yaml (`agents.claude.skill_overrides`,
  `denied_tools`). Web search, Exa, context7 and Playwright stay — research
  subagents depend on them.
- Plugin skills ignore `skillOverrides` (`enabledPlugins` owns them), and
  `disableBundledSkills` is unused because it also drops the review skills.
  `/code-review ultra` and `claude --cloud` have no disable knob; both are
  user-invoked only.

## Cross-model bridge on pi (decision 2026-09-23)

- The `pi` MCP entry spawns `scripts/pi-bridge.mjs` from the chezmoi source
  repo, which runs the repo-local pi in `--mode json` print mode. Tools:
  `review`, `advise`, `reply`; invocation fixed to the read-only tool
  allowlist (`read,grep,find,ls`), `--no-context-files`, no extensions except
  the bridge's own path guard, model (top worker tier) and effort pinned by `agent_mcp_servers.pi` in
  agents.yaml — callers pick scope only. `review`
  embeds a bridge-computed git diff because the child cannot run git.
- MCP transport kept deliberately: the bridge is harness-spawned outside the
  Bash sandbox (the `~/.pi` deny stays intact) and its rendered allow rule
  (`mcp__pi`) makes the tools prompt-free in plan mode (verified 2026-09-23).
  Plan mode blocks MCP tools unless allow-listed (`readOnlyHint` ignored; upstream #12368 closed "not
  planned") and Bash has no plan-mode exemption.
- Read isolation is the guard extension, not a sandbox: pi's built-in tools
  run in-process, so `scripts/pi-bridge-guard.mjs` rewrites each tool path to
  the vetted canonical path inside `cwd` (which must be a git worktree root)
  and blocks `.env*`. Reversal trigger for the bridge: pi's print mode, tool
  allowlist or `tool_call` blocking regresses, or OpenAI withdraws
  ChatGPT-subscription OAuth from third-party harnesses (sanctioned as of
  2026-09-05) — then the review backend needs a new transport.
